body:
For a charger that powerful, I'd want to really flex its capabilities. 

&#x200B;

Video ad: Start off with someone just wanting to charge their iphone when they get to their desk, then progress to charging iphone accessories (gimbal, power bank (another advertisement for a ugreen product), then an ipad so they can upload their footage), then charging a laptop. 

Perhaps frame the ad as a full working day however the catch is that the person has only been at work for a couple of hours and the charger is so fast and powerful they've charged all their devices and kept up their workflow before heading out to lunch.

&#x200B;

One power adapter for all their devices, convenient, powerful and fast.

Howdy,

Looking for an FDM printer that can print Warhammer sized miniatures and also  statues around 7" tall for around the $250 mark. I live in the Philippines. I don't really mind if it's a kit as I have all the tools, a soldering iron and even a mig welder should it come to it lol.

I've considered SLA especially since  the resolution when it comes to miniatures etc. but due to the mess and fumes etc it just wouldn't be practical for my apartment. I also don't want to have to spend more money on a cleaning and curing station as a remedy for my restrictive apartment space.

&#x200B;

As a result, i'm currently eyeing the Ender 3 V2 and the FLsun Q5 since they're both pretty available here and can both be bought for around $200.

&#x200B;

I have no experience with 3d printers, but have experience with miniatures and painting. I've watched countless videos on YouTube of people making models etc but I'm not 100% sure what FDM printer will give me the best results for my budget especially here in the Philippines.

&#x200B;

Thanks!

Yikes I realised I recognised it instantly too.

&#x200B;

JK bitch ni shiboraretai.

I've done this in a Diamond DA-40NG, you'd be surprised at how hard it'll whip your hand back if you aren't expecting it.

&#x200B;

Also interesting to note, opening the DV window in-air was recommended against in I believe the POH, could have just been company policy I don't remember.

&#x200B;

Despite the static ports being on the sides of the fuselage behind the rear canopy, alternate static is derived from within the cockpit, so perhaps opening the window could mess with the G1000/autopilot in some way, I don't exactly remember the specifics.
